{# goal: Brief the operator on skill execution and proposal cards from the Algedonic review board, keeping self-assessments separate from observed evidence and leaving verdicts to the operator. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    focus_skill:
      type: string
      required: false
    outcome_records: object
    feedback_records: object
    issue_reports: object
    board_cards: array
    board_read_status: string
  output:
    per_skill: array
    proposals_awaiting_decision: array
    signal_gaps: array
    briefing_complete: boolean
visibility: Public
---
[inference]
temperature = 0.2
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "standard"
thinking_budget = "full"

Prepare a gemba-walk briefing from observed skill executions and the one
Algedonic review board. The agent must call `kanban_board_list` to identify
that board and `kanban_task_list` to read its cards; read card comments via
`kanban_task_comments_since` when needed. A missing board or failed read is
unknown, never an empty backlog. This briefing is not a verdict: the operator
judges proposals from their card IDs and evidence, not from self-assessment.

{% if focus_skill %}
Focus skill: {{ focus_skill }}
{% endif %}

## Observed signals

### Skill activation outcomes (`reg_query`, namespace `reg.skill`)
{{ outcome_records | tojson }}

### Operator feedback history (`reg_query`, namespace `reg.skill`)
{{ feedback_records | tojson }}

### Skill-use issue reports (`curator_memory_recall`, entity `skill_use_issue:<skill>`)
{{ issue_reports | tojson }}

### Board lookup and card read status
{{ board_read_status }}

### Algedonic review board cards (IDs, descriptions, comments, criteria, deliverables and status)
{{ board_cards | tojson }}

Return one JSON object with these fields:
```json
{
  "per_skill": [{"skill_id": "...", "activations": {"success": 0, "failure": 0}, "issues": [], "health": "healthy | watch | intervene | unobserved", "evidence": ["record ID"], "question_for_operator": "..."}],
  "proposals_awaiting_decision": [{"card_id": "...", "skill_id": "...", "change": "...", "claimed_benefit": "labelled claim", "observed_evidence": ["record or card evidence"], "missing_evidence": ["..."]}],
  "signal_gaps": [],
  "briefing_complete": true
}
```

Use only actual card IDs and observed records. Include every open proposal card;
never infer a skill's quality from activation success. Report failed or empty
channels in `signal_gaps`. If board lookup or card read failed, set
`briefing_complete` to false and mark the backlog unknown. An empty successful
board read is not a failure. Do not rank, accept, reject or close cards.
